Core mechanics unchanged: Jan 1 snapshot fixes both policy duties for the calendar year; ≥25 triggers disconnecting-from-work + electronic-monitoring obligations (latter from Oct 2022); every revision/new hire triggers 30-day distribution. No new statutory text on “as soon as practicable” or rolling updates. 

Unresolved tension: whether monthly tweaks automatically constitute statutory “revisions” requiring fresh circulation, and whether option wording can override described cadence. My prior lean toward C is reinforced; A remains plausible only under very broad reading of distribution flexibility. Key preserved evidence: threshold measured solely on 1 Jan; D’s 2022 drop eliminates 2023 duty; B/E below threshold throughout.}

